From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 137/137] PC5: video frames are converted on one thread, so a game's
 videos aren't black when the converter's threads can't start (Wine patch
 1006)

---
 ...c-convert-video-frames-on-one-thread.patch | 45 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1006-colorcnv-msvproc-convert-video-frames-on-one-thread.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1006-colorcnv-msvproc-convert-video-frames-on-one-thread.patch b/wine/patches/1006-colorcnv-msvproc-convert-video-frames-on-one-thread.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a023df0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1006-colorcnv-msvproc-convert-video-frames-on-one-thread.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] colorcnv, msvproc: Convert video frames on one thread.
+
+The color converter and the video processor set swscale's "threads"
+option to 0, which starts a thread for each CPU (up to 16) each time an
+input or output format is set. On a PS5 title those threads fail to
+start, so sws_init_context returns AVERROR(EAGAIN) from the Windows
+pthread wrapper and every conversion fails: Sacred 2 Remastered logged
+"color_convert_init ret -11" 643 times and showed its videos black.
+One thread converts a frame fast enough, and starts nothing.
+---
+diff --git a/dlls/colorcnv/color_converter.c b/dlls/colorcnv/color_converter.c
+index 38981e4..3c7c239 100644
+--- a/dlls/colorcnv/color_converter.c
++++ b/dlls/colorcnv/color_converter.c
+@@ -592,7 +592,10 @@ static HRESULT color_convert_init(struct color_convert *impl)
+     video_frame_init_aperture(&impl->output_frame, &impl->output_format);
+ 
+     av_opt_set(impl->context, "sws_flags", "neighbor", 0);
+-    av_opt_set_int(impl->context, "threads", 0, 0);
++    /* One thread: with 0, swscale starts a thread for each CPU each time the format is set,
++     * and on a PS5 title those threads fail to start (EAGAIN), so every frame stayed black
++     * (Sacred 2 Remastered's videos). A frame is converted fast enough without them. */
++    av_opt_set_int(impl->context, "threads", 1, 0);
+     av_opt_set_int(impl->context, "srcw", impl->input_frame.width, 0);
+     av_opt_set_int(impl->context, "srch", impl->input_frame.height, 0);
+     av_opt_set_pixel_fmt(impl->context, "src_format", impl->input_frame.format, 0);
+diff --git a/dlls/msvproc/video_processor.c b/dlls/msvproc/video_processor.c
+index f2ad3e0..ef238c7 100644
+--- a/dlls/msvproc/video_processor.c
++++ b/dlls/msvproc/video_processor.c
+@@ -557,7 +557,10 @@ static HRESULT video_processor_init(struct video_processor *impl)
+     video_frame_init_aperture(&impl->output_frame, impl->input_format);
+ 
+     av_opt_set(impl->context, "sws_flags", "neighbor", 0);
+-    av_opt_set_int(impl->context, "threads", 0, 0);
++    /* One thread: with 0, swscale starts a thread for each CPU each time the format is set,
++     * and on a PS5 title those threads fail to start (EAGAIN), so every frame stayed black
++     * (Sacred 2 Remastered's videos). A frame is converted fast enough without them. */
++    av_opt_set_int(impl->context, "threads", 1, 0);
+     av_opt_set_int(impl->context, "srcw", impl->input_frame.width, 0);
+     av_opt_set_int(impl->context, "srch", impl->input_frame.height, 0);
+     av_opt_set_pixel_fmt(impl->context, "src_format", impl->input_frame.format, 0);
-- 
